hidden\" href=\"/practice\"><div class=\"cinematic-wrap absolute inset-0 ken-burns film-grain\"><img src=\"https://hebbkx1anhila5yf.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/Mountain_pass_trident_twilight_s%E2%80%A6_202608031904_3-IfYvsdxzj6itBxExULqvRbhPJTUDtp.jpeg\" alt=\"Mountain pass with ritual trident under twilight sky — the path of practice\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" draggable=\"false\" class=\"cinematic-img-fill\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none\" style=\"z-index:1;background:linear-gradient(to top, rgba(11,12,16,0.98) 0%, rgba(11,12,16,0.7) 30%, rgba(11,12,16,0.15) 70%, transparent 100%)\"></div><div class=\"absolute pointer-events-none\" style=\"z-index:2;top:-20%;left:30%;width:40%;height:80%;background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(197,160,89,0.04) 0%, rgba(197,160,89,0.01) 40%, transparent 100%);transform:rotate(8deg);filter:blur(40px)\"></div><div class=\"dust-overlay\" style=\"z-index:2\"></div></div><div class=\"scrim-bottom-anchored\"></div><div class=\"relative z-10 h-full flex flex-col justify-end p-8 pb-4 md:p-12 md:pb-12 lg:p-16\"><p class=\"section-label mb-4\">Sadhana Instruments</p><h2 class=\"font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-white leading-[0.95] mb-3 hero-heading tracking-wide\">See Yourself.<br/>Clearly.</h2><p class=\"text-foreground text-base max-w-md editorial-spacing\" style=\"text-shadow:0 1px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.7)\">Breathwork, japa, meditation — tools for inner work.</p></div></a></section><div class=\"max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 py-28 md:py-40\"><div class=\"divider-gold mb-20\"></div><div class=\"max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><p class=\"section-label mb-8\">The Mirror Method</p><p class=\"text-sub-display text-foreground mb-8 engraved-heading\">Your patterns<br/>have names.</p><p class=\"text-editorial max-w-xl mx-auto\">Every emotional loop, every recurring relationship dynamic — they map to ancient sadhanas designed for exactly this.</p></div><div class=\"divider-gold mt-20\"></div></div><div class=\"cinematic-strip\"><div class=\"cinematic-wrap absolute inset-0 ken-burns\"><img src=\"https://hebbkx1anhila5yf.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/Pattern_Intelligence_Rescuer_Per%E2%80%A6_202608061239-Tui9sNCxKR6kPFLjWZatF9zLlenizc.jpeg\" alt=\"Sri Yantra floating above Himalayan peaks at twilight\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" draggable=\"false\" class=\"cinematic-img-fill\"/></div><div class=\"cinematic-strip-overlay\"></div></div><section class=\"relative py-20 md:py-32 section-scrim-dim\"><div class=\"cinematic-wrap film-grain absolute inset-0\"><img src=\"https://hebbkx1anhila5yf.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/Mandala_of_divine_masks_202608061239-DAtTaSltoqS1eWGHl1ycNrqpTVKsz3.jpeg\" alt=\"Forgotten forest shrine draped in mist and ancient light\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" draggable=\"false\" class=\"cinematic-img-fill\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none\" style=\"z-index:1;background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(11,12,16,0.82) 0%, rgba(11,12,16,0.3) 30%, rgba(11,12,16,0.4) 60%, rgba(11,12,16,0.92) 100%)\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none\" style=\"z-index:3;background:radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 60% at 50% 50%, transparent 50%, rgba(0,0,0,0.45) 100%)\"></div></div><div class=\"relative z-10 max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10\"><p class=\"section-label editorial-heading mb-6\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\">Pattern Intelligence</p><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5\" style=\"opacity:0\"><div><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/patterns/the-rescuer\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight mb-2 group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">The Rescuer</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim mb-6 font-mono tracking-wider\">Saving others to avoid the self</p><div class=\"divider-subtle mb-5\"></div><ul class=\"space-y-2\"><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->You feel anxious when others solve their own problems</li><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->Relationships feel one-sided — you give, they take</li><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->You cannot ask for help without guilt</li></ul><div class=\"mt-5 pt-3 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-copper\">YANTRA PATTERN · <!-- -->2<!-- --> SIDDHIS LINKED</span></div></div></a></div><div><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/patterns/the-perfectionist\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight mb-2 group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">The Perfectionist</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim mb-6 font-mono tracking-wider\">Controlling outcomes to control anxiety</p><div class=\"divider-subtle mb-5\"></div><ul class=\"space-y-2\"><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->You procrastinate because starting imperfectly feels like failure</li><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->You micromanage tasks others could handle</li><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->Your inner critic speaks louder than anyone else</li></ul><div class=\"mt-5 pt-3 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-copper\">YANTRA PATTERN · <!-- -->2<!-- --> SIDDHIS LINKED</span></div></div></a></div><div><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/patterns/the-ghost\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight mb-2 group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">The Ghost</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim mb-6 font-mono tracking-wider\">Fading out to avoid conflict</p><div class=\"divider-subtle mb-5\"></div><ul class=\"space-y-2\"><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->You say &quot;I&#x27;m fine&quot; when you are not</li><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->Your preferences feel like impositions on others</li><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->You ghost people rather than express disappointment</li></ul><div class=\"mt-5 pt-3 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-copper\">YANTRA PATTERN · <!-- -->2<!-- --> SIDDHIS LINKED</span></div></div></a></div><div><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/patterns/the-controller\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight mb-2 group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">The Controller</h3><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim mb-6 font-mono tracking-wider\">Gripping tight because letting go feels like dying</p><div class=\"divider-subtle mb-5\"></div><ul class=\"space-y-2\"><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->You feel physical tension when plans change unexpectedly</li><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->You correct people even when it does not matter</li><li class=\"text-sm text-text-secondary font-ui tracking-wide leading-relaxed\">· <!-- -->Delegation feels like abdication</li></ul><div class=\"mt-5 pt-3 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-copper\">YANTRA PATTERN · <!-- -->2<!-- --> SIDDHIS LINKED</span></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"mt-12 text-center\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><a class=\"ghost-cta text-sm\" href=\"/patterns\">Decode All 12 Patterns</a></div></div></section><section class=\"relative py-28 md:py-40\"><div class=\"cinematic-wrap absolute inset-0 film-grain\"><img src=\"https://hebbkx1anhila5yf.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/Ancient_codex_and_dossier_scroll_202608061239_2-iT39hyEIdVx6oWFVugB2sp9Mt9uSOF.jpeg\" alt=\"Forgotten chamber with volumetric god rays illuminating ancient yantras and sacred artifacts\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" draggable=\"false\" class=\"cinematic-img-fill\"/><div class=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none\" style=\"z-index:1;background:linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(11,12,16,0.82) 0%, rgba(11,12,16,0.3) 30%, rgba(11,12,16,0.4) 60%, rgba(11,12,16,0.92) 100%)\"></div><div class=\"dust-overlay\" style=\"z-index:2\"></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none\" style=\"z-index:3;background:radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 60% at 50% 50%, transparent 50%, rgba(0,0,0,0.45) 100%)\"></div></div><div class=\"relative z-10 max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10\"><p class=\"section-label editorial-heading mb-8\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\">From the Akashic Archive</p><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6\" style=\"opacity:0\"><div><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/pranava-japa\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Pranava Japa</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">प्रणव जप — Oṃkāra Repetition</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The contemplative repetition of Oṃ, the primal sound (pranava) held in the Upaniṣads to be the sonic signature of the Absolute. Oṃ is not merely a word — it is held to be the acoustic ground from which all manifestation arises and into which it dissolves. The Māṇḍūkya Upaniṣad devotes its entire twelve verses to unpacking its four quarters: the waking state (A), the dream state (U), the deep-sleep state (M), and the fourth (turīya) — the silence beyond. Patañjali&#x27;s Yoga Sūtras (I.27–28) designate Oṃ as the designator of Īśvara and hold that its repetition dissolves obstacles. This is arguably the single most widely practiced contemplative technique in the Hindu tradition, crossing all sectarian boundaries.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Vedānta / Upaniṣadic</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/gayatri-mantra\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Gāyatrī Mantra</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">गायत्री मन्त्र — Savitṛ Invocation</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A verse from the Ṛgveda (III.62.10) invoking the radiant principle (Savitṛ) to illuminate the intellect — among the most widely transmitted invocations in the tradition. The Gāyatrī meter itself is one of the principal Vedic meters, and this particular verse has become the most recited mantra in all of Hinduism, performed daily by millions at dawn and dusk. The verse addresses Savitṛ — the impeller, the stimulating principle of the sun — requesting that the divine radiance inspire our understanding. Its ubiquity across castes, languages, and sects is unparalleled in the Hindu ritual corpus.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Vedic (Ṛgveda)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/nadi-shuddhi\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Nāḍī Śuddhi</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">नाडी शुद्धि — Channel Purification Breath</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Alternate-nostril breathing (anuloma-viloma) used to balance the lunar (iḍā) and solar (piṅgalā) vital currents before deeper practice. This is the foundational breath technique of the Haṭha Yoga system, prescribed in the Haṭha Yoga Pradīpikā (II.7–14) as the first of the eight kumbhakas. The practice is based on the model that the breath flows predominantly through one nostril at a time, alternating roughly every ninety minutes. Nāḍī Śuddhi actively equalizes this flow, producing a state the texts describe as &#x27;sushumna awakening&#x27; — a balanced, integrated awareness suitable for meditation. Modern research on the nasal cycle and its relationship to hemispheric dominance provides an interesting parallel.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Prāṇāyāma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Haṭha / Rāja Yoga</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"mt-12 text-center\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><a class=\"ghost-cta text-sm\" href=\"/archive\">Browse All 41 Siddhis</a></div></div></section><div class=\"cinematic-strip\"><div class=\"cinematic-wrap absolute inset-0 ken-burns\"><img src=\"https://hebbkx1anhila5yf.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/Ancient_codex_and_dossier_scroll_202608061239_2-iT39hyEIdVx6oWFVugB2sp9Mt9uSOF.jpeg\" alt=\"Vast underground library of ancient manuscripts and golden artifacts\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" draggable=\"false\" class=\"cinematic-img-fill\"/></div><div class=\"cinematic-strip-overlay\"></div></div><section class=\"relative py-20 md:py-28 lg:py-32 bg-deep-black\"><div class=\"relative z-10 max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10\"><div class=\"practice-layout grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 md:gap-16 items-center\"><div><p class=\"section-label mb-6\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\">Practice Now</p><h2 class=\"font-display text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl text-white mb-4 hero-heading tracking-[0.12em] uppercase\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\">Breathe.</h2><p class=\"font-ui text-sm tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-12\" style=\"color:var(--gold-label);text-shadow:0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.8);opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\">Nadi Shuddhi — Channel Purification</p><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:scale(0.96)\"><div class=\"flex flex-col items-center gap-6\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl text-gold\">Nāḍī Śuddhi — Basic</h3><div class=\"relative w-52 h-52 flex items-center justify-center\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 240\" class=\"absolute inset-0 w-full h-full -rotate-90\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"120\" r=\"100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--surface-elevated)\" stroke-width=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"120\" r=\"100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--gold)\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"628.3185307179587\" stroke-dashoffset=\"0\" style=\"transition:stroke-dashoffset 0.4s ease\"></circle></svg><div class=\"w-24 h-24 rounded-full border border-[var(--gold-dim)] flex items-center justify-center\" style=\"transform:scale(1);transition:transform 0.4s ease\"><span class=\"font-ui text-2xl text-gold tabular-nums\">—</span></div></div><p class=\"font-ui text-sm text-text-secondary\">Inhale (left)</p><p class=\"font-ui text-xs text-text-muted\">Cycle <!-- -->1<!-- --> / <!-- -->9</p><button class=\"gold-cta text-sm px-8 py-3\">Begin</button></div></div></div><div class=\"relative\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><div class=\"relative rounded-lg overflow-hidden aspect-[16/10]\" style=\"border:1px solid rgba(212,175,55,0.3);box-shadow:0 8px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.5), 0 0 60px rgba(212,175,55,0.06)\"><div class=\"cinematic-wrap absolute inset-0 film-grain\"><img src=\"https://hebbkx1anhila5yf.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/Ritual_items_arranged_on_altar_202608050655-XqjC9wM9ykNWVURx5dcjwvpASTBaPT.jpeg\" alt=\"Nadi Shuddhi channel purification — subtle energy pathways\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" draggable=\"false\" class=\"cinematic-img-fill\"/></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class=\"relative py-28 md:py-40\"><div class=\"cinematic-wrap film-grain absolute inset-0\"><img src=\"https://hebbkx1anhila5yf.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/Copper_trident_in_stone_courtyard_202608050700-R6LSleO2mZ2oSJEvEgxFkYzBceifIa.jpeg\" alt=\"Copper trident in ancient stone courtyard — the depth of commitment\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" draggable=\"false\" class=\"cinematic-img-fill\"/></div><div class=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none z-[1]\" style=\"background:rgba(0,0,0,0.8)\"></div><div class=\"relative z-10 max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10\"><div class=\"text-center mb-20\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><p class=\"section-label mb-6\">Choose Your Depth</p><h2 class=\"font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl text-white hero-heading tracking-[0.08em]\">Four paths.<br/>One purpose.</h2></div><div class=\"max-w-5xl mx-auto\" style=\"opacity:0\"><div class=\"flex flex-col gap-3\"><div class=\"group relative flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-stretch gap-0\" style=\